{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Information.HochschildH1","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Information.HochschildH1","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Information.OuterDerivationResidue","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Bilinear"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.not_inner_of_hh1Class_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.not_inner_of_hh1Class_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/HochschildH1.lean#L118-L123","doc":"**An outer derivation is a nonzero `HH¹` class (sorry-free).**  Contrapositive\npackaging: if a derivation's class is nonzero it is **not** inner — the precise\nshape of the decision residue `res ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.hh1Class_mem_of_isDerivation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.hh1Class_mem_of_isDerivation","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/HochschildH1.lean#L112-L116","doc":"**A derivation's class lies in `HH¹` (sorry-free).**  The image of `Der(A)` in\n`E/Inn(A)` is exactly `HH1`, so every derivation contributes a class there. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.hh1Class_eq_zero_of_inner","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.hh1Class_eq_zero_of_inner","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/HochschildH1.lean#L105-L110","doc":"**Inner derivations are exactly the trivial classes (sorry-free).**  If `D` is\ninner, its class in `E/Inn` vanishes — the quotient really does kill `Inn(A)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.hh1Class","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.hh1Class","kind":"def","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/HochschildH1.lean#L97-L103","doc":"**The class of a linear map in `E/Inn(A)`.**  For a *derivation* `D` this class\nlands in `HH1` (`hh1Class_mem_of_isDerivation`); the decision residue being\nnonzero (`res ≠ 0`) is exactly: some derivation at the fibre level `H_n(ζ)` has\n**nonzero** class — an outer derivation. (No such class is constructed here;\nPROBE A computes `dim HH1(H₃(ζ)) = 1`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.HH1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.HH1","kind":"def","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/HochschildH1.lean#L90-L95","doc":"**First Hochschild cohomology `HH¹(A) = Der(A)/Inn(A)`**, realized as the\n**image of `Der(A)` in `E/Inn(A)`** — the home of the P-vs-NP decision\nresidue. Because `Inn(A) ≤ Der(A)` (`inner_le_der`), this image is canonically\nthe subquotient `Der/Inn`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.DerivationQuotient","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.DerivationQuotient","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/HochschildH1.lean#L81-L87","doc":"**The endomorphism space modulo inner derivations, `E/Inn(A)`.**  The ambient\nquotient in which `HH¹` is realized. (Working with this ambient quotient\navoids the instance diamond that a linear-map-space *sub*quotient\n`↥Der ⧸ Inn` triggers; since `Inn ≤ Der` the image of `Der` here is\ncanonically `Der/Inn`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.inner_le_der","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.inner_le_der","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/HochschildH1.lean#L73-L78","doc":"**`Inn(A) ≤ Der(A)` (sorry-free).**  Every inner derivation is a derivation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.innerDerivation_isDerivation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.innerDerivation_isDerivation","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/HochschildH1.lean#L69-L71","doc":"**`ad_x` really is a derivation (sorry-free).** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.innerDerivationSubmodule","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.innerDerivationSubmodule","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/HochschildH1.lean#L65-L67","doc":"**The inner-derivation submodule `Inn(A) ⊆ A →ₗ[R] A` (sorry-free).** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.innerMap_eq_innerDerivation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.innerMap_eq_innerDerivation","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/HochschildH1.lean#L60-L62","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.innerMap_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.innerMap_apply","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/HochschildH1.lean#L57-L58","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.innerMap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.innerMap","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/HochschildH1.lean#L52-L55","doc":"**Inner derivations as an `R`-linear map `x ↦ ad_x`.**  Built from the\nmultiplication bilinear map, so it is linear in `x` for free; its range is the\nsubmodule `Inn(A)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.mem_derivationSubmodule","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.mem_derivationSubmodule","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/HochschildH1.lean#L48-L49","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.derivationSubmodule","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.derivationSubmodule","kind":"def","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/HochschildH1.lean#L34-L46","doc":"**The derivation submodule `Der(A) ⊆ A →ₗ[R] A` (sorry-free).**  Closed under\n`0`, `+`, and `R`-scalars — the scalar case uses `smul_mul_assoc` /\n`mul_smul_comm` (the algebra scalar slides through the product). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.IsDerivation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.IsDerivation","kind":"def","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/HochschildH1.lean#L30-L31","doc":"**`D` is a derivation** — the associative-algebra Leibniz rule. ","signatureChunk":0}]}